{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Six days may work be done.</b> See — during the six days of work you are able to do the labor of the Tabernacle. If so, it is not fitting that the Sabbath be pushed aside on its account, for no commandment overrides the Sabbath unless it has a fixed time and that time falls on the Sabbath, such as the sacrificial service and circumcision. But when it is possible to fulfill the commandment on another day, it does not override the Sabbath at all." "<b>Sabbath of solemn rest.</b> See — even a matter that is not included among the categories of prohibited labor is forbidden on it, as it says: וּבַיּוֹם הַשְּׁבִיעִי תִּשְׁבֹּת (Exodus 23:12). This is so that it be <b>holy to HaShem</b> — so that man on it turn entirely away from transient life to engage in the pursuits of eternal life, to the honor of his Creator." "<b>Whoever does work shall be put to death.</b> And therefore it is just that one who nullifies this intent by doing work shall be put to death."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:44.119155648Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}